+Retrieval is hybrid and scope-bounded. Exact identifiers and structured
+constraints are resolved first and are never displaced by a learned model.
+Otherwise Thunderbird unions lexical, dense, sender, entity, template, and
+thread candidates, fuses the retrieval lists with reciprocal-rank fusion,
+then optionally scores the bounded candidate set with the selected learned
+reranker. Only the final evidence cards enter the context budget. A reranker
+failure degrades to deterministic field-aware ordering; it does not widen the
+scope or prevent lexical retrieval. Non-loopback rerankers receive only
+policy-redacted query and evidence text.
+
+When an identifier query resolves to exactly one record, Thunderbird locks that
+record and renders its canonical subject, amount, date, merchant, reference,
+sender, and message source locally. This exact-field path does not ask an
+endpoint to restate or replace those values. The trace records the exact lock
+and the local renderer so a source URI or an endpoint abstention can never be
+mistaken for field-level evidence.
 
