+Backfill uses `mail.ai.backfill.batch_size`,
+`mail.ai.backfill.max_queue`, `mail.ai.backfill.scan_chunk`, and
+`mail.ai.backfill.checkpoint_interval`. Balanced-mode defaults are
+`batch_size=5`, `max_queue=200`, `scan_chunk=400`, and
+`checkpoint_interval=25`. Checkpoints resume after the last committed message
+and workers/timers terminate at completion.
+
+Canonical generated AI state is stored row-by-row in
+`ai/mail-intelligence.sqlite`. The schema separates message records, mailbox
+digest records, provider state, mining state, and bounded global sections.
+Writes use WAL, deferred transactions, and changed-record checkpoints; a
+backfill therefore updates the affected rows instead of serializing the whole
+mailbox. On first startup after upgrade, a valid legacy
+`ai/mail-intelligence.json` is imported in bounded chunks and retained as
+`ai/mail-intelligence.pre-sqlite.json` only after the SQLite import commits.
+An interrupted import leaves the legacy file authoritative and retries safely.
+
+Exact folder, account, and all-mail rollups are accelerated by a separate,
+disposable profile-local SQLite index at `ai/rag-index.sqlite`. A monotonically
+increasing record generation invalidates this derived index after analysis
+changes. Normal message changes are applied incrementally; bulk resets or
+missed generations trigger a lazy rebuild. Later requests reuse the cached
+scope rollup without rescanning every AI record. Selected-message rollups stay
+ephemeral. Runtime diagnostics report source/index generations, rebuild state,
+FTS availability, cache hits, and records scanned. Deleting only the RAG index
+is safe because Thunderbird rebuilds it from canonical
+`mail-intelligence.sqlite` records.
 
